{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And the harp.</b> Known." "<b>Nevel.</b> It has ten holes. Also ḥalil is from the root חלל (hollow)." "<b>And the work of YHWH they do not regard.</b> After the manner of the many who are occupied with drunkenness — they do not know the ways of HaShem; likewise all who stray in it will not be wise (Proverbs 20:1). In my opinion, in this place he speaks only of the evils that HaShem brought upon Israel, for the tens of the tribes were exiled."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:06.655881145Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}